      <h1 id="oadp-use-cases-backup" class="group scroll-mt-20">Backup using OpenShift API for Data Protection and Red Hat OpenShift Data Foundation (ODF) <a href="#oadp-use-cases-backup" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">Following is a use case for using OADP and ODF to back up an application.</p>
      <h2 id="oadp-usecase-backup-odf_oadp-use-cases-backup" class="group scroll-mt-20">Backing up an application using OADP and ODF<a href="#oadp-usecase-backup-odf_oadp-use-cases-backup" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">In this use case, you back up an application by using OADP and store the backup in an object storage provided by Red Hat OpenShift Data Foundation (ODF).</p>
      <ul>
      <li>You create an object bucket claim (OBC) to configure the backup storage location. You use ODF to configure an Amazon S3-compatible object storage bucket. ODF provides MultiCloud Object Gateway (NooBaa MCG) and Ceph Object Gateway, also known as RADOS Gateway (RGW), object storage service. In this use case, you use NooBaa MCG as the backup storage location.</li>
      <li>You use the NooBaa MCG service with OADP by using the <code>aws</code> provider plugin.</li>
      <li>You configure the Data Protection Application (DPA) with the backup storage location (BSL).</li>
      <li>You create a backup custom resource (CR) and specify the application namespace to back up.</li>
      <li>You create and verify the backup.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You installed the OADP Operator.</li>
      <li>You installed the ODF Operator.</li>
      <li>You have an application with a database running in a separate namespace.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create an OBC manifest file to request a NooBaa MCG bucket as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: objectbucket.io/v1alpha1\nkind: ObjectBucketClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: test-obc\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  storageClassName: openshift-storage.noobaa.io\n  generateBucketName: test-backup-bucket"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>test-obc</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the object bucket claim.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>test-backup-bucket</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the bucket.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the OBC by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <obc_file_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;obc_file_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the file name of the object bucket claim manifest.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      When you create an OBC, ODF creates a <code>secret</code> and a <code>config map</code> with the same name as the object bucket claim. The <code>secret</code> has the bucket credentials, and the <code>config map</code> has information to access the bucket. To get the bucket name and bucket host from the generated config map, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc extract --to=- cm/test-obc"} lang="terminal" />
      <p><code>test-obc</code> is the name of the OBC.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"# BUCKET_NAME\nbackup-c20...41fd\n# BUCKET_PORT\n443\n# BUCKET_REGION\n\n# BUCKET_SUBREGION\n\n# BUCKET_HOST\ns3.openshift-storage.svc"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To get the bucket credentials from the generated <code>secret</code>, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc extract --to=- secret/test-obc"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\nebYR....xLNMc\n# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\nYXf...+NaCkdyC3QPym"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Get the public URL for the S3 endpoint from the s3 route in the <code>openshift-storage</code> namespace by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get route s3 -n openshift-storage"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a <code>cloud-credentials</code> file with the object bucket credentials as shown in the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"[default]\naws_access_key_id=<AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID>\naws_secret_access_key=<AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>cloud-credentials</code> secret with the <code>cloud-credentials</code> file content as shown in the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create secret generic \\\n  cloud-credentials \\\n  -n openshift-adp \\\n  --from-file cloud=cloud-credentials"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Configure the Data Protection Application (DPA) as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionApplication\nmetadata:\n  name: oadp-backup\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  configuration:\n    nodeAgent:\n      enable: true\n      uploaderType: kopia\n    velero:\n      defaultPlugins:\n        - aws\n        - openshift\n        - csi\n      defaultSnapshotMoveData: true\n  backupLocations:\n    - velero:\n        config:\n          profile: \"default\"\n          region: noobaa\n          s3Url: https://s3.openshift-storage.svc\n          s3ForcePathStyle: \"true\"\n          insecureSkipTLSVerify: \"true\"\n        provider: aws\n        default: true\n        credential:\n          key: cloud\n          name:  cloud-credentials\n        objectStorage:\n          bucket: <bucket_name>\n          prefix: oadp"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>defaultSnapshotMoveData</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Set to <code>true</code> to use the OADP Data Mover to enable movement of Container Storage Interface (CSI) snapshots to a remote object storage.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>s3Url</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the S3 URL of ODF storage.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;bucket_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the bucket name.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the DPA by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f <dpa_filename>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Verify that the DPA is created successfully by running the following command. In the example output, you can see the <code>status</code> object has <code>type</code> field set to <code>Reconciled</code>. This means, the DPA is successfully created.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get dpa -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nitems:\n- apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\n  kind: DataProtectionApplication\n  metadata:\n    namespace: openshift-adp\n    #...#\n  spec:\n    backupLocations:\n    - velero:\n        config:\n          #...#\n  status:\n    conditions:\n    - lastTransitionTime: \"20....9:54:02Z\"\n      message: Reconcile complete\n      reason: Complete\n      status: \"True\"\n      type: Reconciled\nkind: List\nmetadata:\n  resourceVersion: \"\""} lang="yaml" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Verify that the backup storage location (BSL) is available by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get backupstoragelocations.velero.io -n openshift-adp"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME           PHASE       LAST VALIDATED   AGE   DEFAULT\ndpa-sample-1   Available   3s               15s   true"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Configure a backup CR as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: velero.io/v1\nkind: Backup\nmetadata:\n  name: test-backup\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  includedNamespaces:\n  - <application_namespace>"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;application_namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the namespace for the application to back up.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the backup CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f <backup_cr_filename>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the backup object is in the <code>Completed</code> phase by running the following command. For more details, see the example output.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc describe backup test-backup -n openshift-adp"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"Name:         test-backup\nNamespace:    openshift-adp\n# ....#\nStatus:\n  Backup Item Operations Attempted:  1\n  Backup Item Operations Completed:  1\n  Completion Timestamp:              2024-09-25T10:17:01Z\n  Expiration:                        2024-10-25T10:16:31Z\n  Format Version:                    1.1.0\n  Hook Status:\n  Phase:  Completed\n  Progress:\n    Items Backed Up:  34\n    Total Items:      34\n  Start Timestamp:    2024-09-25T10:16:31Z\n  Version:            1\nEvents:               <none>"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
